error[ffi_not_constant]: `fixedbugs-2075-calls.h` has `C_PAIR`, but not as a constant — clang cannot read its value while compiling
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-2075-a-record-whose-leaf-calls-undefined-arithmetic-is-refused.hero:17:5
     |
  17 |     constant C_PAIR: Pair  #~ ffi_not_constant
     |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  note: a `constant` names one value forever (§4.4), and clang reads `C_PAIR` as something computed each time it is read, an object, a call or a statement expression it does not fold, so nothing holds two reads of it to one answer: the mutable global §4.2 forbids. A value computed in C is reached through a function of the program's own that returns it, written in a header beside this file and bound by `extern` naming that header like any function: `static inline <its C type> hero_C_PAIR(void) { <its C type> value = C_PAIR; return value; }`
